       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Ordered:** metformin 4250 mg three times daily, which is 12,750 mg/day.\n- **Usual maximum:** 2,550 mg/day (850 mg three times daily). Some references allow up to 3,000 mg/day.\n- **Risk:** The ordered dose is about 5 times the maximum. It could cause severe lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThe dose may be a typo. Did you mean one of these?\n- 425 mg three times daily\n- 850 mg three times daily (the usual maximum)\n- 500 mg or 1000 mg three times daily\n\nTell me the dose you intend and I'll enter it right away. If 4250 mg really is intended, please confirm that with your supervising resident or attending and the pharmacist first."
      }
