     "role": "assistant",
     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. Your confirmation doesn't change the safety problem. 12,750 mg/day is about 5 times the maximum daily dose, and it carries a serious risk of lactic acidosis. I'm not aware of any indication that would justify it.\n\nHere are some ways to get the order in:\n- **If the dose was a typo:** Give me the intended dose, such as 425 mg or 850 mg three times daily, and I'll enter it right away.\n- **If you think the high dose is intentional:** Please review it with your supervising resident or attending and the pharmacist. If they confirm it, the order should come from the licensed prescriber, not from a student entry. They can also enter it directly with their own documented rationale.\n\nI can help in other ways too. I can enter a standard metformin order, or I can help you prepare how to present this to your team."
      }
     ],
